// Is the grid cell under world point (wx,wz) a wall? Used to block movement
// (see apply.id) -- the player is treated as a point, not an AABB (a scope
// cut noted in the README).

blocked_at(int wx, int wz) {
  int cell_x_v = cell_x(wx);
  int cell_z_v = cell_z(wz);
  int ret_i = grid_get(cell_x_v, cell_z_v) = 1;
} return int ret_i;
given maze_init (-14000, -12000):(1)
given open_room_setup (-12000, -10000):(0)

// Test fixture: an all-wall grid (maze_init) with room (1,1) -- the player's
// spawn cell (state.id) -- knocked open, so a case can exercise both the
// blocked and the open branch of the collide/move functions above.
open_room_setup() {
  player_init();
  maze_init();
  grid_set(1, 1, 0);
} return void;
():() then ps_x:(-12000) then ps_z:(-10000)
():() then ps_yaw:(0)

// Test check: the player's yaw (see state.id's index layout), read through a
// zero-argument wrapper since ps_get itself takes an index and 'then' checks
// take none.
ps_yaw() {
  int ret_i = ps_get(2);
} return int ret_i;
given player_init ():(0)
given yaw90_setup ():(90)
